2Co 11:1 , Out of his jealousy over the Corinthians, who seemed to make more account of the false apostles than of him, he enters into a forced commendation of himself
2Co 11:5 , of his equality with the chief apostles
2Co 11:7 , of his preaching the gospel to them freely, and without any charge to them;
2Co 11:13 , shewing that he was not inferior to those deceitful workers in any legal prerogative;
2Co 11:23 , and in the service of Christ, and in all kinds of sufferings for his ministry, far superior.
